---
description: "Project conventions (always on)"
alwaysApply: true
---

Project conventions. Always apply.

- Branches: feature branches only; `feat/<task-id>-slug`,
  `fix/<task-id>-slug`, `chore/<task-id>-slug`.
- Commits: Conventional Commits (`feat(scope): …`, `fix(scope): …`).
  Subject line ≤ 72 chars; body explains the *why* when not obvious.
- PRs/MRs: link the task; one approval and a green pipeline are required
  before merge.
- Update shared contract files (OpenAPI, protobuf, schema) in the same
  change that modifies the interface.
- Add or update tests with every behavior change; new modules need a
  sibling test file mirroring the task id when reasonable.
- Update user-facing docs (`docs/runbook.md`, README, etc.) when operator
  or user behavior changes.
- No AI attribution, agent branding, or "generated by" lines in commits.
